name: Complete file enumeration stays distinct from partial content inspection
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=@ART/empty-git-config GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=@ART/empty-git-config KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_completeness.py seed @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
keys: C-g
require-live-snap: 20 COMMAND PALETTE | palette
type: scopes
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Enter / c build inventory | empty-inventory
keys: c
require-live-snap: 30 DRAFT SCOPES | bounded-inventory
expect: Inventory limited: true
expect: File enumeration: complete
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_completeness.py draft @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 File enumeration: | coverage
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 complete under inventory policy | coverage-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 complete under inventory policy | coverage-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 File enumeration: | coverage-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 File enumeration: | coverage-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 File enumeration: | coverage-40x12
expect: complete under
keys: NPage
live-snap: coverage-read-40x12
ask: Are completed file enumeration and limited content inspection distinct, with the coverage details readable at all six sizes and no complete source-analysis claim?
resize: 120x36
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Accept exact boundaries | acceptance
keys: End Enter
require-live-snap: 25 inventory limitations require explicit acknowledgement | acknowledgement-required
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_completeness.py refused @TMP_TARGET @ART
keys: Home Enter End Enter
require-live-snap: 25 ACCEPTED SCOPES | acknowledged-boundaries
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_completeness.py accepted @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does acceptance require the separate inventory-limit acknowledgement, preserve the whole-repository boundary and start no scan, model request or allowance?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=@ART/empty-git-config GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM=@ART/empty-git-config NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
keys: C-g
require-live-snap: 20 COMMAND PALETTE | restart-palette
type: scopes
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 ACCEPTED SCOPES | restored-inventory
expect: File enumeration: complete
expect: Inventory limited: true
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_completeness.py restarted @TMP_TARGET @ART
ask: Does no-color restart retain the accepted boundaries and both completeness facts without rebuilding inventory or creating work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
